  "narrative": {
    "intro": "CACI Federal reported $2.8B in contract obligations for FY2026 to date. CACI Federal won 216 awards this fiscal year to date. CACI Federal has an average award size of $12.9M. Obligations are down 20.9% year over year. Historical obligations show growth through FY25, with figures of $1.3B in FY21, $1.7B in FY22, $2.3B in FY23, $2.8B in FY24, and $3.5B in FY25 before the current-year total of $2.8B. The Department of Defense is the largest buying agency, obligating $1.5B to CACI Federal this fiscal year to date, followed by the General Services Administration at $950M and the Department of Homeland Security at $215M. Computer Systems Design Services and Engineering Services are the top NAICS markets for CACI Federal, at $1.1B and $648M respectively, with a mix of investigations, R&D, and other professional services making up the remainder of obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are CACI Federal's biggest buyers this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.5B to CACI Federal in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $950M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $215M. Additional buying agencies include the National Aeronautics and Space Administration at $135M and the Department of the Interior at $26.4M. The Department of Justice obligated $5M and the Department of Commerce obligated $1.1M; the Department of Health and Human Services shows $0."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What services and markets generate most of CACI Federal's obligations?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services generated $1.1B in obligations for CACI Federal this fiscal year to date. Engineering Services generated $648M. Other leading markets include Investigation and Personal Background Check Services at $258M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $231M. Additional services with notable obligations include All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $192M and Other Computer Related Services at $118M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does CACI Federal make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "CACI Federal has $2.8B in contract obligations FY2026 to date. CACI Federal won 216 awards so far this fiscal year and the average award size is $12.9M. Obligations are down 20.9% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from CACI Federal?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense, General Services Administration, Department of Homeland Security, National Aeronautics and Space Administration, Department of the Interior, Department of Justice, Department of Commerce, and Department of Health and Human Services buy from CACI Federal. The Department of Defense obligated $1.5B, the General Services Administration obligated $950M, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $215M in FY2026 to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does CACI Federal sell to the government?",
      "a": "CACI Federal sells services in Computer Systems Design Services, Engineering Services, Investigation and Personal Background Check Services, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences, and a range of other professional and technical services. Computer Systems Design Services generated $1.1B and Engineering Services generated $648M in FY2026 to date, with Investigation and Personal Background Check Services at $258M and R&D at $231M."
